OpenAI started selling the ModRetro Chromatic: Codex Edition, a $200 retro handheld, on Nov. 9 through its Supply Co. merchandise store. Per OpenAI's product page, buyers add the ModRetro Chromatic plugin to Codex, describe a game and the agent builds a ROM that can be streamed to the handheld or written to the included cartridge. VGTimes reported that Codex works in GB Studio and draws the sprites. OpenAI first gave the device to about 2,500 attendees of its Sept. 29 DevDay, Generation Amiga reported.

The DevDay swag is now a $200 Supply Co. product, and the game studio behind it is a prompt to Codex.

